14. CRITICAL — New VehicleList record

This is the most important part of your requirement.

When creating the estimate:

Logged-in user
      ↓
SBCES.Users.Department
      ↓
SBCES.VehicleList.Department

Do not accept Department from the browser for this operation.

Instead, query the logged-in user.

For example:

private async Task<string> GetCurrentUserDepartmentAsync()
{
    var userADId = User?.Identity?.Name;

    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(userADId))
    {
        throw new UnauthorizedAccessException(
            "Unable to determine logged-in user.");
    }

    const string sql = @"
        SELECT Department
        FROM SBCES.Users
        WHERE UserADId = @UserADId;
    ";

    var department =
        await _dbConnection.QuerySingleOrDefaultAsync<string>(
            sql,
            new { UserADId = userADId });

    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(department))
    {
        throw new UnauthorizedAccessException(
            "Logged-in user does not have a Department.");
    }

    return NormalizeDepartment(department);
}
Important

If your AD authentication returns a value such as:

DOMAIN\jsmith

while Users.UserADId contains:

jsmith

then adjust this one lookup to match your actual authentication claim.

Do not take Department from JavaScript or the posted VehicleViewModel when creating an estimate.

